"""
## Purpose and audience
Covers the drafted `tee` CLI tool contract (TOOL-TEE): text read from a
source is passed through unchanged while being mirrored into line-shaped
file output. Audience: tools maintainers and the CLI feature backlog.
## Operator workflow
Run this spec from the repo root with the Simple runner. Green means the
drafted API is still absent and nothing has silently replaced it; when an
implementation lands, these scenarios must be ported onto the real entry
point before this spec can honestly pass.
## Compatibility and limitations
No tee implementation exists anywhere under src/ (census verified
2026-09-06), so scenario one asserts the documented absence instead of
calling an invented oracle. Runtime pass-through behavior cannot be
asserted yet.
## Verification guidance and troubleshooting
A failure of the absence tripwire means a tee implementation now exists:
port both scenarios to drive the real tool, record its pass-through text
and split line counts as captures, and drop the tripwire.
"""
# Lifecycle: doc/01_research/domain/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ;
# doc/03_plan/sspec_modernization_plan.md ;
# doc/04_architecture/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ;
# doc/05_design/infra/sspec/modern_sspec_typed_evidence_design.md
# @manual_section: tee-tool-contract

# NOTE: defect — no tee tool exists anywhere under src/ (census over
# src/app and src/lib found no tee entry point, 2026-09-06). The drafted
# TOOL-TEE feature has no backing module, so scenario one is a fail-closed
# absence tripwire instead of a call to an invented oracle. Unblock: land
# the tool, then port both scenarios onto the real entry point.
use std.spec.*
use std.spec.step
use std.io_runtime.file_exists

describe "tee tool":
    context "basic functionality":
        it "passes text through":
            # @req REQ-TOOL-TEE
            # @capture(statistics): tee implementation absence census
            step("Probe the tree for any drafted tee tool entry point")
            val tee_impl_present = file_exists("src/app/tools/tee.spl") or file_exists("src/app/tools/tee/main.spl")
            expect(tee_impl_present).to_be(false)  # oracle: the TOOL-TEE feature is unimplemented; true would mean the spec must be ported before it can pass

        it "splits text into lines for file output":
            # @req REQ-TOOL-TEE
            # @capture(statistics): line-shaped mirror output for the fixture text
            step("Split the fixture text on newlines with the stdlib text API")
            val content = "line1\nline2\nline3"
            val lines = content.split("\n")
            expect(lines.len()).to_equal(3)  # oracle: the fixture text has three newline-separated lines
